/// TLS service (`tls`, issue 103, Appendix B.6): TLS 1.3 client sessions over the client's own network flow. A client
/// lends its network stack capability (`attach`), so the network policy that applies to the client applies to its TLS
/// connections too; the service holds no network access of its own. Server certificates are verified against the root
/// store `tlsroots.pem` on the boot disk. With `client-certificate`, the device certificate is offered when a server
/// asks for one and the key service signs the handshake: the TLS service never sees the private key. A session belongs
/// to the process that attached it; the service runs one handshake at a time. 1.1 adds `connect-pinned`: a server known
/// by its key alone, such as the update server (351-NET-0002).
package mind:tls@1.1.0;

interface tls {
    /// Why a request failed. `certificate`: the server certificate is not valid for the name or not trusted;
    /// `handshake`: the handshake failed otherwise; `no-entropy`: the processor has no RDRAND (the service fails
    /// closed); `no-roots`: no usable root certificate.
    enum error { no-network, refused, timeout, closed, again, invalid, limit, not-found, denied, certificate, handshake, no-entropy, no-roots }

    /// An established session: the cipher suite and key exchange group (IANA numbers), whether the device certificate
    /// was sent.
    record peer { suite: u16, group: u16, client-certificate: bool }

    /// A new session on the client's network flow (its socket client, idl/socket.wit).
    attach: func(flow: borrow<endpoint>) -> result<u32, error>;
    /// TCP to `address`:`port`, then the TLS 1.3 handshake verifying the server for `name` (a DNS name or an IPv4
    /// address in dotted form).
    connect: func(session: u32, name: string<253>, address: u32, port: u16, client-certificate: bool, timeout-ms: u32) -> result<peer, error>;
    /// Encrypts and sends `data`; returns how many bytes were taken.
    send: func(session: u32, data: bytes<4096>) -> result<u32, error>;
    /// Up to `length` decrypted bytes. Error again: nothing yet; closed: the peer closed and everything was read.
    receive: func(session: u32, length: u32) -> result<bytes<4096>, error>;
    /// Sends close_notify, closes the connection and frees the session and the lent flow.
    close: func(session: u32) -> result<_, error>;
    /// The device certificate (DER), from the key service.
    certificate: func() -> result<bytes<512>, error>;
    /// As `connect`, the server verified by its key alone (1.1): the SHA-256 of its certificate's SubjectPublicKeyInfo
    /// must be `pin` (32 bytes), or the connection is refused (`certificate`). No root, name or validity period is
    /// checked; the handshake's signature by that key is. `name` is sent as the server name.
    connect-pinned: func(session: u32, name: string<253>, address: u32, port: u16, pin: bytes<32>, timeout-ms: u32) -> result<peer, error>;
}
